-- title:
--   Layer propagation of smooth-point stalks, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Arithmetic frame.** Fixed are: a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 3$; a level $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, characterised by the hypothesis that $w \in W$ holds exactly when $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. $w$ is rational (the structure map from the base field to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and its value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in the set `ssJSet q`; an element $s$ of $W$; the inclusion hypothesis $\mathrm{hle}$ asserting `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, where the former is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full-level-$M'$ modular function field and the latter is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the analogous base change of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the base-changed full-level field equipped with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, such that a constant lies in the integers exactly when it lies in $A$, the residue map is compatible with reduction of constants, every nonzero element becomes an integer with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with the order functions on divisors; and the hypothesis $\mathrm{hR}_0$: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Field of constants.** Fixed are an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is a henselian local ring, and has algebraically closed residue field; and the hypothesis $\mathrm{h\kappa}$: every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and elements.** Fixed are a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0$ of $k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** Fixed are a type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$ (an element of $K_n$ lies in $A_n$ precisely when its image lies in $A$); a base layer $K_b$ with the hypothesis $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ likewise cut out by $A$, and a nonzero element $\varpi_b$ of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equip `fieldBar q M'` with the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. The assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that
--
--   (i) the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, and
--
--   (ii) (linear disjointness) for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$: if $c$ is linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i\,a_i = 0$ in `fieldBar q M'`, then all $a_i = 0$;
--
--   and for every field $F_{ss}$ which is an algebra over the residue field of $A$, every regular prolongation $R$ of type `RegularProlongation A ↥(fieldBar q M') FSS` (a valuation subring `R.integers` of `fieldBar q M'` with a surjective residue homomorphism to $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, cutting out $A$ on constants, compatible with reduction of constants, and with the scaling property), subject to the hypothesis that an element of $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` exactly when it lies in $W_0$; and for every finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$, every family $S_b$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by such places, families $\varphi_b(Q) : A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q) : S_b(Q) \to$ `ResidueField A` of ring homomorphisms, and a family $D_b(Q)$ of sets of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — if the following base-layer hypothesis holds:
--
--   $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements; for every place $Q \notin N$: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ is that image; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in the residue field of $A$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ carries a local ring structure for which the kernel of $\chi_b(Q)$ is the maximal ideal; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and conversely every element $f$ of that join satisfies $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_b(Q)$ with $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and of essentially finite type; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in `R.integers` and an element $f$ of $S_b(Q)$ lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` exactly when $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$ divides $f$; for every $f \in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of the places $P$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and for which $A$-valuation of the $P$-value of $f$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$; moreover: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, a place $P$ belonging to both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$ forces $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_b(Q)$ the order at $P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the Laurent series `jq` of $j$ (transported along $\mathrm{hle}$) is $\ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and every witness $\mathrm{h\tau}$ that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, and every place $Q$: the translate of $Q$ by the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` lies in $N$ iff $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then `smulDisc τ (Db Q)` $= D_b(\mathtt{R.resAut τ hτ} \cdot Q)$, where `smulDisc τ D` is $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D\}$ —
--
--   then there exist families $S_n(Q, n)$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q,n) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n) : S_n(Q,n) \to$ `ResidueField A`, and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   First, $N$ has $q+1$ elements, and for every place $Q \notin N$:
--
--   (1) for every layer $n$: the reduction map $A_n \to$ `ResidueField A` is surjective; the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_n$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)$ equals that image; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ which is a section of $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$, satisfies that the residue of $\chi(f)$ is $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$ for all $f$, and sends $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ to $c$; for every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$, $f$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; $D_n(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and such that the $A$-valuation of the $P$-value of $f$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_n(Q,n)(f) = 0$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) \neq \varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,c)$ for every $c \in A_n$; $S_n(Q,n)$ carries a local ring structure whose maximal ideal is the vanishing locus of $\chi_n(Q,n)$, and is a Noetherian ring and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$, and every element $f$ of that join satisfies $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_n(Q,n)$ with $h \neq 0$; the linear-disjointness clause of (ii) holds with $K'$ replaced by $K_n$; every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ which is a section of $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$ and induces $\chi_n(Q,n)$ on residues has kernel the principal ideal generated by $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) - \varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)))$; there exists a nonzero $\varpi \in A_n$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_n(Q,n)$, such that an element $f$ of the join above lies in `R.integers` exactly when $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_n(Q,n)$ with $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ satisfies $f\,h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$;
--
--   (2) (layer compatibility) there is a witness that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q,n) \le S_n(Q,n')$, and moreover: for $K_n \le K_{n'}$, $S_n(Q,n')$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ have one and the same image in `fieldBar q M'` for all $n, n'$; and for $K_n \le K_{n'}$ the map $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricts on $S_n(Q,n)$ to $\chi_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   Second, for $Q, Q' \notin N$, a layer $n$ and a place $P$ belonging to both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$, one has $Q = Q'$.
--
--   Third, for $Q \notin N$, every layer $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$, the order at $P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the Laurent series `jq` (transported along $\mathrm{hle}$) is $\ge 0$.
--
--   Fourth, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every witness that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, and every place $Q$: the translate of $Q$ by `R.resAut τ hτ` lies in $N$ iff $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $= D_n(\mathtt{R.resAut τ hτ} \cdot Q, n)$ for every layer $n$.
--
--   Fifth, for every $Q \notin N$ and every layer $n$, $S_b(Q) \le S_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   Sixth, for every $Q \notin N$, every layer $n$ and every place $P$, membership of $P$ in $D_b(Q)$ implies membership in $D_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   This is the layer-propagation step for the semistable model of the full-level modular curve at $q$ in the case $q = 3$ under the rigidifying hypothesis that a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ divides the auxiliary level: étale charts (stalks with coordinate, residue character and residue discs) at the smooth points of the supersingular fibre, given over the base layer $k_0$, are extended over every finite layer $K_n$, compatibly in $n$ and containing the base-layer charts and discs. It feeds the assembly of the supersingular prolongation with its ends, residue discs and node data.
